Found the issue! The problem is with the **double quotes** in your Zephyr template. Zephyr in Email Composer doesn't support double quotes.

Here's the corrected syntax with single quotes:

```zephyr
{if profile.vars.tier == 'gold'}
  <p>Hi {name}, your gold rewards are ready.</p>
{else}
  <p>Hi {name}, welcome back.</p>
{/if}

{foreach content as c}
  <a href="{c.url}">{c.title}</a>
{/foreach}
```

**Changes made:**
- `"gold"` → `'gold'` (single quotes instead of double quotes)

According to Sailthru's documentation: *"Use single quotes in Email Composer so your Zephyr renders properly."* Double quotes are not supported in Email Composer and will cause errors.
